        "target": "Given:\n- Each tire can hold 500 cubic inches of air.\n- Two tires are completely empty.\n- One tire is 40% full.\n- One tire is 70% full.\n- Each pump adds 50 cubic inches of air.\n\nFirst, calculate the air needed for the empty tires:\n- 2 empty tires need 500 cubic inches each, so \\(2 \\times 500 = 1000\\) cubic inches.\n\nNext, calculate the air needed for the partially filled tires:\n- The 40% full tire needs \\(500 - (500 \\times 0.4) = 500 - 200 = 300\\) cubic inches.\n- The 70% full tire needs \\(500 - (500 \\times 0.7) = 500 - 350 = 150\\) cubic inches.\n\nTotal air needed:\n- \\(1000 + 300 + 150 = 1450\\) cubic inches.\n\nSince each pump adds 50 cubic inches:\n- Number of pumps needed = \\(1450 / 50 = 29\\).\n\nFINAL: 29",
